oracle GNU Make 4.4.1
outcome success
file %.c kept 1
| bare
file Makefile kept 16
| # GNU Make's `enter_prereqs` (file.c) compresses a static pattern rule's
| # percent escaping into a COPY of the prerequisite and throws the copy away
| # when no wildcard survived it — `percent = find_percent (nm); if (percent)
| # ... dp->name = ...` — so a prerequisite pattern that is not a pattern reaches
| # the build spelt exactly as the makefile wrote it, backslash and all.
| #
| # `\%.c` holds no wildcard, so it names one file called `\%.c` for both
| # targets. `\\%.c` does hold one — an even run of backslashes halves and the
| # `%` survives — so it stands for `\a.c` and `\b.c`.
| all: a.o b.o a.q
| 
| a.o b.o: %.o: \%.c
| 	@cat '$<' > $@
| 
| a.q: %.q: \\%.c
| 	@cat '$<' > $@
file \%.c kept 1
| escaped
file \a.c kept 1
| one-backslash
file a.c kept 1
| no-backslash
file a.o touched 1
| escaped
file a.q touched 1
| one-backslash
file b.o touched 1
| escaped
